# Which runner the app talks to. Read at build time (it also sets the CSP connect-src).
#   mock                     in-memory mock runner and chain, no network requests at all (default)
#   self                     the runner serves this app from the same origin
#   https://runner.example   a runner on another origin
#   http://xyz.onion         a runner behind a Tor onion service
#   runners                  an app host: talks to exactly the runners in VITE_RUNNERS
#                            (comma-separated origins, all added to connect-src), using
#                            VITE_DEFAULT_RUNNER for pages without a runner of their own
VITE_API=mock
# VITE_RUNNERS=https://sandbox.example,https://main.example
# VITE_DEFAULT_RUNNER=https://sandbox.example

# Which signer the app ships. Read at build time.
#   mock   in-memory stand-in with no real cryptography (default)
#   wasm   the real cadence-core signer in Web Workers; run `pnpm build:wasm` first,
#          and point VITE_API at a real runner (it registers pockets with POST /api/pockets)
VITE_SIGNER=mock
